The copairing composed on the right with the left injection is the first of the two maps.

If the composite relates an input to an output, an intermediate sum neighbourhood is a left copy of that input and is related by the copairing. A master output is the master relation of the first map, a left copy shrinks to the given relation, and a right copy cannot contain the left copy. Conversely, the left copy of the input is an intermediate neighbourhood whose copairing clause is that same left copy.
